  "instruction": "Open VSCode with ~/projects/rust-wasm. Set up a Rust WebAssembly project: (1) Install wasm-pack: 'curl https://rustwasm.github.io/wasm-pack/installer/init.sh -sSf | sh'. (2) Update Cargo.toml: set crate-type=['cdylib', 'rlib'], add wasm-bindgen dependency. (3) Update src/lib.rs to export a greet(name: &str) -> String function using #[wasm_bindgen] attribute. Add a fibonacci(n: u32) -> u32 function and export it. (4) Run 'wasm-pack build --target web' to generate the pkg/ directory. (5) Create a simple www/index.html and www/index.js that import the generated WASM module and call greet() and fibonacci(). (6) Create .vscode/tasks.json with a 'WASM: Build' task running wasm-pack build and a 'WASM: Serve' task running a simple HTTP server. Add the wasm file extension to .vscode/settings.json file associations.",
